  "vegSub": "PCT 2 · River Red Gum–sedge very tall open forest in frequently flooded forest wetland · Riverina, south-western NSW",
  "intro": "Before 1750 your address stood in very tall River Red Gum forest on the frequently flooded floodplain around Moulamein — trees often thirty metres high and more, lining channels, billabongs and low backplains that filled with each flood. Shrubs are naturally sparse here; the life of the forest floor is a carpet of sedges, rushes, flood-loving grasses and wildflowers that wake each time the water arrives. It is nesting country for waterbirds, and it has been assessed as Vulnerable, with dieback since 2000. The plants below are indigenous to this community and its higher, drier edges, grouped by the layer they fill. Plant the canopy first; the sedges and herbs belong in the damp ground beneath it.",
